{#- The approval page: the one place a scope is granted, and the press design.md §12
    ("A scope is a press that lasts", 2026-09-22) rests on.

    It is the sign-in page's family — the lockup, one card on the desk, no navigation —
    because it is the same kind of moment: somebody is in the middle of something that
    started somewhere else, and a page with three ways off it would be three ways to
    lose them. It reuses `signin.css` and adds only the scope list.

    Two things on this page are load-bearing rather than decorative. The client's name is
    said as the client's claim about itself, because dynamic registration means a
    stranger wrote it. And the spending scope says what it costs, in credits with the rate
    beside them (§12, 2026-09-23), because a standing grant that did not say so would be a
    worse seam than the press it replaces. -#}
<!doctype html>
<html lang="{{ page_language|default('en') }}">
<head>
<meta charset="utf-8">
<meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
<title>targum</title>
{% include '_icons.html.j2' %}
<style>{{ asset('reader.css') }}{{ asset('signin.css') }}</style>
{{ hebrew_face() }}
{{ chrome_face() }}
</head>
<body class="signin">
<main class="gate">
  <a class="brand" href="/" aria-label="targum">
    <svg class="brand-mark" viewBox="20 12 56 72" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false">
      <rect x="20" y="12" width="22" height="62" rx="5" fill="currentColor"></rect>
      <rect x="54" y="22" width="22" height="62" rx="5" fill="var(--mark-accent)"></rect>
    </svg>
    <span>targum</span>
  </a>

  <div class="door">
    <h1>{{ t("connect.page.connect-to-targum", "Connect {client} to targum", client=client) }}</h1>
    <p class="said">{{ t("connect.page.this-is-what-it-would-be-able-to-do", "This is what it would be able to do.") }}</p>

    <ul class="scopes">
      {%- for scope in scopes %}
      <li>
        {#- Through the catalogue, not straight off `oauth.SCOPES`. The three scopes are
            written in that module as English and were drawn here raw, so a Russian
            reader met the whole page in their own language except the three lines that
            say what they are agreeing to (2026-09-23). `tests/test_oauth.py` holds the
            English here and there to the same words. -#}
        <span class="scope-says">{{ t("connect.scope." + scope.name, scope.says) }}</span>
        {#- The rate travels with the number, every time it is shown (§12, 2026-09-23):
            a credit the reader has to convert from memory is the invented currency §6
            forbids, and a credit with its equivalence beside it is a minute with a
            better name. -#}
        {%- if scope.name == 'chat' %}
        <span class="scope-cost">{{ t("connect.page.uses-your-credits", "Uses your {credits} credits — about {hours} hours of audio", credits=credits, hours=hours) }}</span>
        {%- endif %}
      </li>
      {%- endfor %}
    </ul>

    {%- if spends %}
    {#- Said once, in words, above the button. A reader who grants this is agreeing to
        spending that happens later without another press, and the page they agree on is
        the only place that can tell them so. -#}
    <p class="said">{{ t("connect.page.we-read-the-hebrew-you-write", "We read the Hebrew you write and keep what you got wrong. A message is a few seconds, so it barely touches your credits, and everything else you say there is yours and costs none of them.") }}</p>
    {%- endif %}

    <form method="post" action="/oauth/authorize">
      <input type="hidden" name="asked" value="{{ query }}">
      <button class="go" type="submit" name="press" value="approve"><span class="go-says">{{ t("connect.page.connect", "Connect") }}</span><svg class="go-arrow" viewBox="0 0 16 16" aria-hidden="true" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2.2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round"><path d="M3 8h10M9 4l4 4-4 4"/></svg></button>
      <button class="ghost" type="submit" name="press" value="refuse">{{ t("connect.page.not-now", "Not now") }}</button>
    </form>

    <p class="aside">{{ t("connect.page.you-can-disconnect-it-later", "You can disconnect it whenever you like, from your account.") }}</p>
    <p class="aside">{{ t("connect.page.it-will-come-back-to", "It will come back to {redirect}", redirect=redirect) }}</p>
  </div>
</main>
</body>
</html>
